(begin-tx "TX-EQSS-04 - a stale class-3 base is SEEN and REPAIRED (the other half of the fix)")
(print "")
(print "=== TX-EQSS-04 — deb-staleness is blind to it; the re-rate engine is not =====")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== TX-EQSS-04 - stale class-3 base seen and repaired · 01 · let / invocation ====
(print "--- [TX-EQSS-04 · 01 · let / invocation] ---")
;;WHY THIS USES CustodiansPool AND NOT THE EQUITY POOL. With the share doors gated, an equity
;;base can no longer BE driven stale through any client path -- which is the point of the gate and
;;also why the repair half needs a different lever to test. The SF SCORE DEFINITION is that
;;lever: `AQP-SCR|C_IssueSemiFungibleScoreDefinition` re-weighs a nonce through `WW_SFScore`,
;;which is an UPSERT with no emptiness check, so it re-values a live position exactly the way a
;;share issuance used to. Same class-3 base, same corruption, and this one is still OPEN -- it is
;;the sibling hole the share-count audit turned up, recorded here as a TEST rather than a note.
(let
    (
        (anhd:string KST.ANHD)
        (dhoc:string "DHOC-98c486052a51")
        (ref-U|DALOS:module{UtilityDalosV2} U|DALOS)
        (ref-AQP:module{AcquisitionPoolsV3} AQP-POOL)
        (ref-SCR:module{AcquisitionScoresV7} AQP-SCORE)
        (ref-TS02-C3:module{TalosStageTwo_ClientThreeV8} TS02-C3)
    )
    (let
        (
            (pool-id:string (ref-U|DALOS::UDC_Makeid "CustodiansPool"))
        )
        ;;THE FIXTURE IS DISCOVERED, NOT NAMED. CustodiansPool employs a bronze/silver/golden
        ;;triplet and each member weighs ONE nonce, so which score carries a given holder's weight
        ;;is a property of the boot, not something a test should assert by spelling. Naming
        ;;`OuronetPrimeBronze` picked a score whose weight for the held nonce is 0.0, and the test
        ;;then "passed" its way into an out-of-bounds read on an empty work list.
        (let
            (
                (weighted:[string]
                    (filter
                        (lambda (sid:string)
                            (> (ref-SCR::UR_U-SCR|UserScoreBaseScore anhd pool-id sid) 0.0))
                        (ref-AQP::URC_PoolActiveScoreIds pool-id)))
                (rows:[object] (ref-AQP::URH_AQP|ActiveDpsfTrackerRows pool-id dhoc))
            )
            (enforce (> (length weighted) 0)
                "TX-EQSS-04 needs a class-3 score carrying real weight for ANHD in CustodiansPool")
            (enforce (> (length rows) 0)
                "TX-EQSS-04 needs a live DHOC position in CustodiansPool")
        (let
            (
                (score-id:string (at 0 weighted))
                (nonce:integer (at "nonce" (at 0 rows)))
            )
        (let
            (
                (val-pre:decimal (ref-SCR::UR_S-DEF|SFScoreNonceScoreValue score-id dhoc nonce))
                (base-pre:decimal (ref-SCR::UR_U-SCR|UserScoreBaseScore anhd pool-id score-id))
                (owner:string (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreOwnerKonto score-id))
            )
            (print (format "<(discovered)> => score {} weighs nonce {}" [score-id nonce]))
            (map print
                [
                    (format "<(definition value for the held nonce)> => {}" [val-pre])
                    (format "<(ANHD stored base)> => {}" [base-pre])
                    (expect (format "<<TX-EQSS-04>> pre: a position carries weight got={}" [base-pre])
                        true (> base-pre 0.0))
                    (expect (format "<<TX-EQSS-04>> pre: engine reports no work got={}"
                            [(ref-AQP::URHC_AQP|ScoreBackfillOutstanding pool-id score-id)])
                        0 (length (ref-AQP::URHC_AQP|ScoreBackfillOutstanding pool-id score-id)))
                ]
            )
            ;;==== TX-EQSS-04 - stale class-3 base · 02 · the route is now REFUSED ====
            (print "--- [TX-EQSS-04 · 02 · halving a nonce weight under a live stake is REFUSED] ---")
            ;;THIS TRANSACTION USED TO MANUFACTURE THE DEFECT, AND NOW PINS ITS CLOSURE. Until
            ;;2026-11-08 it halved a nonce's definition weight WHILE ANHD held a staked position,
            ;;then showed that (a) the stored base was wrong, (b) `UserScoreDebStale` was blind to
            ;;it, and (c) `CCp_BackfillScoreSlice` could see and repair it. That demonstration is
            ;;gone because the vector is gone: `SCR|C>ISSUE-SF-SCORE-DEFINITION` now carries the
            ;;`nzs-count = 0` + `not drift-locked` gate its three reconfiguration siblings always
            ;;had (owner ruling 2026-11-08 — a weight change does not re-value positions already
            ;;staked, so the score must be vacated first).
            ;;
            ;;WHAT THE OLD ASSERTIONS PROVED IS NOT LOST, IT IS RELOCATED. The claim "deb-staleness
            ;;cannot see a base error" is a property of `URC_U-SCR|UserScoreDebStale` — it
            ;;recomputes the DERIVED layers FROM the stored base, so a base error moves neither
            ;;side of its comparison — and it is still asserted below against a HEALTHY row, which
            ;;is the only state now reachable. What can no longer be exhibited is a stale class-3
            ;;base, because after PureV25 gated the equity-share vector and this round gated the
            ;;definition vector, NO client entrypoint can produce one.
            (env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
            (map print
                [
                    ;;THE REFUSAL, BY ITS MESSAGE. ANHD signs and names the score's real owner, so
                    ;;neither the executor binding nor the ownership keyset can be what rejects
                    ;;this — the reconfiguration gate is the only thing left that can. (CLAUDE.md,
                    ;;"authorisation precedes validation": choose the fixture that gets past the
                    ;;first guard, or the test passes with the new guard deleted.)
                    (expect-failure (format "<<TX-EQSS-04>> re-issuing nonce {} under a LIVE stake is REFUSED — vacate to reconfigure" [nonce])
                        "the score must have no stakers (nzs-count = 0) — vacate to reconfigure — and the score must not be drift-locked"
                        (ref-TS02-C3::AQP-SCR|C_IssueSemiFungibleScoreDefinition
                            anhd owner score-id dhoc [nonce] [(/ val-pre 2.0)]))
                    ;;AND NOTHING MOVED. An `expect-failure` proves the transaction aborted, not
                    ;;that the definition is untouched — a guard placed after a write would abort
                    ;;just as loudly while leaving the row changed.
                    (expect (format "<<TX-EQSS-04>> the definition value is UNCHANGED by the refused call got={}" [val-pre])
                        val-pre (ref-SCR::UR_S-DEF|SFScoreNonceScoreValue score-id dhoc nonce))
                    (expect (format "<<TX-EQSS-04>> ...and so is the stored base got={}" [base-pre])
                        base-pre (ref-SCR::UR_U-SCR|UserScoreBaseScore anhd pool-id score-id))
                ]
            )
            (env-sigs [])
            ;;==== TX-EQSS-04 - stale class-3 base · 03 · the engine agrees the row is healthy ====
            (print "--- [TX-EQSS-04 · 03 · the engine agrees the row is healthy] ---")
            ;;THE RE-RATE ENGINE IS NOT DEAD CODE, AND THIS IS WHERE THAT IS RECORDED. With both
            ;;class-3 vectors gated it has nothing left to repair FOR CLASS 3 — matching the live
            ;;chain, where `URHC_AQP|ScoreBackfillOutstanding` returns 0 for all 8 supported
            ;;(pool, score) pairs (SCAN-2026-11-08-live.md §1). Its remaining purpose is class 4,
            ;;whose model-0 weight reads `DPDC-S::URC_N|Score` LIVE and is moved by a different
            ;;role holder in a module deployed BEFORE 02_SCORE — so a gate at the write site is
            ;;architecturally impossible there and detect-and-repair is the only available answer
            ;;(SPEC-class4-score-revaluation.md).
            (let
                (
                    (outstanding:[object] (ref-AQP::URHC_AQP|ScoreBackfillOutstanding pool-id score-id))
                    (deb-stale:bool (ref-SCR::URC_U-SCR|UserScoreDebStale anhd pool-id score-id))
                )
                (map print
                    [
                        (format "<(AQP-POOL|URHC_…ScoreBackfillOutstanding)> => {}" [outstanding])
                        (format "<(AQP-SCORE|URC_…UserScoreDebStale)> => {}" [deb-stale])
                        (expect (format "<<TX-EQSS-04>> the engine reports NO work — the gate held got={}" [(length outstanding)])
                            0 (length outstanding))
                        (expect (format "<<TX-EQSS-04>> deb-staleness also reports fresh got={}" [deb-stale])
                            false deb-stale)
                    ]
                )
            )
            ;;==== TX-EQSS-04 - stale class-3 base · 04 · a slice on a healthy score is a safe no-op ====
            (print "--- [TX-EQSS-04 · 04 · a slice on a healthy score is a safe no-op] ---")
            ;;WORTH ASSERTING RATHER THAN ASSUMING. The repair route stays deployed and callable by
            ;;the pool owner, so "what happens if someone runs it when nothing is wrong" is a real
            ;;question with a money answer. It must drive the base to the canonical target, and on
            ;;a healthy row the target IS the stored value — so the slice must change nothing.
            (env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
            (print (format "<(AQP-POOL|CCp_BackfillScoreSlice)> => \"{}\""
                [(ref-TS02-C3::AQP-POOL|CCp_BackfillScoreSlice anhd pool-id score-id [anhd])]))
            (env-sigs [])
            (let
                (
                    (base-post:decimal (ref-SCR::UR_U-SCR|UserScoreBaseScore anhd pool-id score-id))
                    (outstanding-post:[object] (ref-AQP::URHC_AQP|ScoreBackfillOutstanding pool-id score-id))
                )
                (map print
                    [
                        (format "<(ANHD base)> => {} -> {}" [base-pre base-post])
                        (expect (format "<<TX-EQSS-04>> the slice is a NO-OP on a healthy row got={}" [base-post])
                            base-pre base-post)
                        (expect (format "<<TX-EQSS-04>> the sweep still CONVERGES -- no work left got={}" [outstanding-post])
                            0 (length outstanding-post))
                        (expect (format "<<TX-EQSS-04>> base never went negative got={}" [base-post])
                            false (< base-post 0.0))
                    ]
                )
            )
        )
        )
        )
    )
)
(commit-tx)
;;||>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
;;|| NEXT                   >
;;||>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
(print "")
;;================================================================================
(begin-tx "TX-EQSS-05 - a DRIFT-LOCKED score refuses a definition re-issue, on BOTH arms")
(print "")
(print "=== TX-EQSS-05 — the drift latch now reaches the definition writers ==================")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 900000000)(env-gas 0)
;;THE SECOND CONJUNCT, TESTED WHERE IT IS NOT SHADOWED. <<TX-EQSS-04>> exercises the same enforce
;;but on a score WITH stakers, so `nzs-count = 0` fails first and the drift clause is never
;;evaluated — delete `(not (UR_SCR|ScoreDriftLocked score-id))` and that test stays green. Both
;;scores here are EMPTY, so `nzs-count` passes and the latch is the only thing that can refuse.
;;(CLAUDE.md, "authorisation precedes validation": two state-dependent guards in one enforce expose
;;only one at a time, and the fix is a second fixture rather than a reordering.)
;;
;;AND IT COVERS BOTH GUARD SITES. The guard lives in exactly two capabilities, not four:
;;`SCR|C>ISSUE-SF-SCORE-DEFINITION` for class 3, and `SCR|XI>X_ISSUE-NF-SCORE-DEFINITION` — which
;;BOTH NF entry caps (trait mode and set mode) `compose-capability` — for class 4. The set-mode arm
;;is driven below; trait mode reaches the identical clause through the same composed capability.
;;
;;WHY THE LATCH MATTERED MORE THAN THE EMPTINESS CHECK. `SCR|C>LOCK-SCORE-DRIFT` is the strongest
;;promise the module makes about weights — fully built, with field, reader, writer, entrypoint,
;;`URCi_` and migration — and until 2026-11-08 NOT ONE definition writer consulted it. A score
;;explicitly promised drift-proof could still have its per-nonce weights re-issued underneath its
;;holders.
(let
    (
        (ref-TS02-C3:module{TalosStageTwo_ClientThreeV8} TS02-C3)
        (ref-SCR:module{AcquisitionScoresV7} AQP-SCORE)
        ;;
        (patron:string KST.ANHD)
        (coding-id:string "TheCodingDivision-98c486052a51")
        ;;THE CLASS-4 FIXTURE TOOK TWO CORRECTIONS, AND BOTH ARE SHADOWING TRAPS. It must be
        ;;EMPTY, LOCKABLE, and employed by a pool that stakes the very collectable the definition
        ;;names:
        ;;  - naming a collectable the pool does NOT stake is refused by an earlier validator
        ;;    ("…would score nothing"), which would shadow the latch and pass §04 for the wrong
        ;;    reason — hence `DHB`, the DHBloodshed pool's asset, and not `KBN`;
        ;;  - `SubsidiaryBloodshed` is NOT lockable ("deb-boost must be off and boost-class-link
        ;;    must be BAR"), so §03 aborted on it. `Bloodshed` satisfies both.
        (bloodshed-id:string "Bloodshed-98c486052a51")
        (dhcd-id:string "DHCD-98c486052a51")
        (kbn-id:string "DHB-98c486052a51")
    )
    ;;==== TX-EQSS-05 · 01 · precondition — both scores EMPTY and UNLOCKED ====
    (print "--- [TX-EQSS-05 · 01 · precondition — both scores EMPTY and UNLOCKED] ---")
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<TX-EQSS-05>> fixture: class-3 score is EMPTY and UNLOCKED, so only the latch can refuse it"
                [3 0 false]
                [(ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreClass coding-id)
                 (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreNzsCount coding-id)
                 (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreDriftLocked coding-id)])
            (expect "<<TX-EQSS-05>> fixture: class-4 score is EMPTY and UNLOCKED too"
                [4 0 false]
                [(ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreClass bloodshed-id)
                 (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreNzsCount bloodshed-id)
                 (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreDriftLocked bloodshed-id)])
        ]
    )
    ;;==== TX-EQSS-05 · 02 · baseline — while UNLOCKED both arms ACCEPT a re-issue ====
    (print "--- [TX-EQSS-05 · 02 · baseline — while UNLOCKED both arms ACCEPT a re-issue] ---")
    ;;THE HALF THAT PROVES THE GATE IS NOT A BLANKET REFUSAL. Without it, a guard that rejected
    ;;every re-issue unconditionally would pass §04 identically.
    (env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<TX-EQSS-05>> SF arm: an empty, unlocked score ACCEPTS a definition re-issue"
                7.5
                (let ((_:string (ref-TS02-C3::AQP-SCR|C_IssueSemiFungibleScoreDefinition
                                    patron (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreOwnerKonto coding-id)
                                    coding-id dhcd-id [11] [7.5])))
                    (ref-SCR::UR_S-DEF|SFScoreNonceScoreValue coding-id dhcd-id 11)))
            (expect "<<TX-EQSS-05>> NF arm (set mode): likewise ACCEPTED while unlocked"
                true
                (!= "" (ref-TS02-C3::AQP-SCR|C_IssueNonFungibleSetScoreDefinition
                           patron (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreOwnerKonto bloodshed-id)
                           bloodshed-id kbn-id [0] [1.0])))
        ]
    )
    ;;==== TX-EQSS-05 · 03 · latch both scores ====
    (print "--- [TX-EQSS-05 · 03 · latch both scores] ---")
    (ref-TS02-C3::AQP-SCR|C_LockScoreDrift patron (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreOwnerKonto coding-id) coding-id)
    (ref-TS02-C3::AQP-SCR|C_LockScoreDrift patron (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreOwnerKonto bloodshed-id) bloodshed-id)
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<TX-EQSS-05>> both scores are now drift-locked, and still EMPTY"
                [true true 0 0]
                [(ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreDriftLocked coding-id)
                 (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreDriftLocked bloodshed-id)
                 (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreNzsCount coding-id)
                 (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreNzsCount bloodshed-id)])
        ]
    )
    ;;==== TX-EQSS-05 · 04 · THE LATCH REFUSES BOTH ARMS — the assertions that fail without F1 ====
    (print "--- [TX-EQSS-05 · 04 · THE LATCH REFUSES BOTH ARMS] ---")
    (map print
        [
            (expect-failure "<<TX-EQSS-05>> SF arm: a drift-locked score REFUSES a definition re-issue"
                "the score must have no stakers (nzs-count = 0) — vacate to reconfigure — and the score must not be drift-locked"
                (ref-TS02-C3::AQP-SCR|C_IssueSemiFungibleScoreDefinition
                    patron (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreOwnerKonto coding-id) coding-id dhcd-id [11] [9.5]))
            (expect-failure "<<TX-EQSS-05>> NF arm: the SHARED composed capability refuses it too"
                "the score must have no stakers (nzs-count = 0) — vacate to reconfigure — and the score must not be drift-locked"
                (ref-TS02-C3::AQP-SCR|C_IssueNonFungibleSetScoreDefinition
                    patron (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreOwnerKonto bloodshed-id) bloodshed-id kbn-id [0] [2.0]))
            ;;AND THE REFUSED WRITE LEFT NOTHING BEHIND — an abort proves the tx failed, not that
            ;;the row is intact; a guard placed after the write would abort just as loudly.
            (expect "<<TX-EQSS-05>> the SF definition still holds the value set while unlocked"
                7.5 (ref-SCR::UR_S-DEF|SFScoreNonceScoreValue coding-id dhcd-id 11))
        ]
    )
    (env-sigs [])
)
(print "===^^^===")
(commit-tx)
;;||>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
;;|| NEXT                   >
;;||>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
(print "")
;;================================================================================
(begin-tx "TX-EQSS-06 - the re-rate engine can now ANSWER for a class-4 (DPNF) score")
(print "")
(print "=== TX-EQSS-06 — class 4 enters the re-rate engine =================================")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 900000000)(env-gas 0)
;;WHAT WAS WRONG WAS NOT A WRONG ANSWER, IT WAS AN INDISTINGUISHABLE ONE. Until 2026-11-09
;;`URC_AQP|ScoreBackfillSupported` fenced class 4 out, and `URHC_AQP|ScoreBackfillOutstanding`
;;returns `[]` for an unsupported score BY DESIGN -- its own @doc says so, and reads empty as fully
;;rated. So a class-4 score reported exactly like a clean one whether it was clean or whether the
;;engine was refusing to look.
;;
;;THAT IS NOT A CORNER OF THE SYSTEM. Measured against mainnet 2026-11-08: FIVE of the fifteen live
;;scores are class 4 -- Bloodshed, SubsidiaryBloodshed, SubsidiaryBunnies, SubsidiaryNosferatu,
;;NosferatuDracula -- spanning FOUR of the eight live pools. A third of the live surface had no
;;staleness detector at all and read as healthy.
;;
;;THE ASSERTION THAT ACTUALLY PROVES THE NEW TARGET IS `outstanding = 0` ON A SCORE WITH A LIVE
;;STAKER. `delta = target - stored base` per holder, so an empty work list on a staked score says
;;the new `URH_AQP|ScoreTargetBaseForBeneficiaryNf` reproduces what the STAKE path wrote -- for the
;;real holder, through the real DPNF tracker rows. Had it summed per nonce instead of handing the
;;whole vector over once, or used the DPSF tracker, or mis-rounded the integer amounts, this would
;;be non-empty. Support alone would not have shown that: a wrong target is "supported" too.
(let
    (
        (ref-SCR:module{AcquisitionScoresV7} AQP-SCORE)
        (ref-AQP:module{AcquisitionPoolsV3} AQP-POOL)
        ;;
        (pool:string "DHBunnies-98c486052a51")
        (score:string "SubsidiaryBunnies-98c486052a51")
    )
    ;;==== TX-EQSS-06 · 01 · fixture — a class-4 score WITH a live staker ====
    (print "--- [TX-EQSS-06 · 01 · fixture — a class-4 score WITH a live staker] ---")
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<TX-EQSS-06>> fixture: class 4, employed by its pool, and NOT empty (a staker exists)"
                [4 pool true]
                [(ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreClass score)
                 (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreAqpoolLink score)
                 (> (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreNzsCount score) 0)])
        ]
    )
    ;;==== TX-EQSS-06 · 02 · the engine now SUPPORTS it — the assertion that fails without F2 ====
    (print "--- [TX-EQSS-06 · 02 · the engine now SUPPORTS it] ---")
    (map print
        [
            ;;BEFORE 2026-11-09 THIS WAS `false`. The fence read `[0 1 3]`.
            (expect "<<TX-EQSS-06>> class 4 is now SUPPORTED by the re-rate engine"
                true
                (ref-AQP::URC_AQP|ScoreBackfillSupported pool score))
            ;;AND THE LEG SCAN REACHES THE RIGHT TRACKER. A class-4 pool holds a COLLECTABLE, so
            ;;`URC_AQP|PoolLiquidityLegs` cannot be asked about it -- the branch is taken before
            ;;that reader, and it must pick the DPNF tracker rather than the DPSF one. Non-empty
            ;;`nat-rows` is what says it did; empty frz/slp is what says it did not fall through
            ;;to the liquidity path.
            (expect "<<TX-EQSS-06>> the leg scan reads the DPNF tracker — nat-rows populated, no liquidity legs"
                [true 0 0]
                (let ((lr:object (ref-AQP::URH_AQP|ScoreBackfillLegRows pool)))
                    [(> (length (at "nat-rows" lr)) 0)
                     (length (at "frz-rows" lr))
                     (length (at "slp-rows" lr))]))
        ]
    )
    ;;==== TX-EQSS-06 · 03 · the new target REPRODUCES the stake path ====
    (print "--- [TX-EQSS-06 · 03 · the new target REPRODUCES the stake path] ---")
    ;;THE LOAD-BEARING ASSERTION, AND IT CALLS THE TARGET DIRECTLY ON PURPOSE.
    ;;
    ;;`URHC_AQP|ScoreBackfillOutstanding` ALONE CANNOT PROVE THIS, and that is the finding itself:
    ;;it returns `[]` for an UNSUPPORTED score, so "no work" passes identically whether the target
    ;;is right or whether the engine is refusing to look. Measured -- reverting the fence to
    ;;`[0 1 3]` turned the SUPPORT assertion above red and left the work-list assertion GREEN. A
    ;;test built only on the work list would certify the defect.
    ;;
    ;;So the target is invoked through `URH_AQP|ScoreTargetBaseForBeneficiary`, the DISPATCHER,
    ;;which consults the score class and NOT the fence -- and its answer is compared to the base
    ;;the STAKE path actually wrote. That equality is false if the class-4 arm sums per nonce
    ;;instead of handing the whole vector over once, reads the DPSF tracker, or mis-rounds the
    ;;integer amounts; and it cannot be satisfied by refusing to answer.
    (let*
        (
            (leg-rows:object (ref-AQP::URH_AQP|ScoreBackfillLegRows pool))
            (holders:[string] (ref-AQP::URHC_AQP|ScoreBackfillCandidates pool score leg-rows))
            (outstanding:[object] (ref-AQP::URHC_AQP|ScoreBackfillOutstanding pool score))
        )
        (enforce (> (length holders) 0) "TX-EQSS-06 needs at least one class-4 holder to compare")
        (let
            (
                (who:string (at 0 holders))
            )
            (map print
                [
                    (format "<(holders)> => {}" [(length holders)])
                    (format "<(AQP-POOL|URHC_…ScoreBackfillOutstanding)> => {}" [outstanding])
                    ;;the discriminating one: TARGET == STORED BASE, via the dispatcher
                    (expect (format "<<TX-EQSS-06>> the class-4 TARGET equals the base the stake path wrote got={}"
                            [(ref-SCR::UR_U-SCR|UserScoreBaseScore who pool score)])
                        (ref-SCR::UR_U-SCR|UserScoreBaseScore who pool score)
                        (ref-AQP::URH_AQP|ScoreTargetBaseForBeneficiary
                            pool score who
                            (at "nat-rows" leg-rows) (at "frz-rows" leg-rows) (at "slp-rows" leg-rows)))
                    ;;...and it is a REAL figure, not a vacuous 0 == 0
                    (expect (format "<<TX-EQSS-06>> ...and that base is NON-ZERO, so the equality is not 0 == 0 got={}"
                            [(ref-SCR::UR_U-SCR|UserScoreBaseScore who pool score)])
                        true (> (ref-SCR::UR_U-SCR|UserScoreBaseScore who pool score) 0.0))
                    (expect (format "<<TX-EQSS-06>> the work list is consequently empty got={}" [outstanding])
                        0 (length outstanding))
                    (expect "<<TX-EQSS-06>> ...and the cheap predicate agrees with the work list"
                        false (ref-AQP::URHC_AQP|ScoreBackfillNeeded pool score))
                ]
            )
        )
    )
    ;;==== TX-EQSS-06 · 04 · class 2 is STILL fenced out, deliberately ====
    (print "--- [TX-EQSS-06 · 04 · class 2 is STILL fenced out, deliberately] ---")
    ;;THE FENCE IS NOT NOW OPEN TO EVERYTHING. Class 2 (DPOF) weighs per-nonce amounts through a
    ;;different pair of functions and has no target of its own, so admitting it would compute a
    ;;delta from the wrong formula -- which does not fail, it writes a plausible wrong number into
    ;;a maintained accumulator. Asserted as a NEGATIVE so that opening the fence further has to be
    ;;a deliberate act that turns this line red.
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<TX-EQSS-06>> the supported-class list is exactly [0 1 3 4] — class 2 is refused"
                [true true true true false]
                (map (lambda (c:integer) (contains c [0 1 3 4])) [0 1 3 4 2]))
            ;;F10's CLASS-2 BOUND IS **NOT** BEHAVIOURALLY TESTED HERE, AND SAYING SO IS THE POINT.
            ;;
            ;;`URC_AQP|ScoreMxChangeSafe` short-circuits to `true` for every class whose asset has no
            ;;`DPTF|PropertiesTable` row -- freezing and sleeping are variants of a FUNGIBLE. Classes
            ;;3 and 4 were lifted out on 2026-10-10; class 2 (DPOF) was left inside the scanning
            ;;branch, where it reaches `ref-DPTF::UR_Frozen` on an ortofungible id and ABORTS. The
            ;;bound was corrected `> 2` -> `> 1` on 2026-11-09.
            ;;
            ;;THERE IS NO CLASS-2 POOL TO TEST IT AGAINST -- not in any fixture and not on mainnet.
            ;;Measured: the fixture tree holds classes 0, 1, 3 and 4; the eight live pools likewise.
            ;;An earlier version of this block asserted `URC_AQP|ScoreMxChangeSafe` on a CLASS-4
            ;;score and claimed to be testing the class-2 branch. A mutation round caught it:
            ;;reverting the bound to `> 2` left this suite GREEN, because class 4 short-circuits
            ;;under both bounds. The assertion looked behavioural and proved nothing.
            ;;
            ;;SO WHAT IS ASSERTED IS THE BOUND ITSELF, labelled as such: every collectable class
            ;;must be short-circuited, and the two liquidity classes must not be. That IS a
            ;;regression detector on the constant -- it goes red if the bound moves again -- and it
            ;;is NOT evidence that the class-2 path executes correctly. Making it such evidence
            ;;needs a DPOF pool fixture, recorded as the open item in FINDINGS-2026-11-08.md F10.
            (expect "<<TX-EQSS-06>> F10 bound: collectable classes 2/3/4 short-circuit, liquidity classes 0/1 do not"
                [false false true true true]
                (map (lambda (c:integer) (> c 1)) [0 1 2 3 4]))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(print "===^^^===")
(commit-tx)
(print "")
(print "================================================================")
(print "EQUITY-SHARE-STALENESS END")
(print "================================================================")
